{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/176270-a-thought-on-vampiric-population","id":176270,"title":"A Thought on Vampiric population","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-21T12:28:09-07:00","id":176270,"title":"A Thought on Vampiric population","content":"I was reading through the Ordo Dracul Covenant book and thought once again how rather thin my city's covenant is. For that matter, all the existing covenants are relatively insipid, since there are so few members of each. And I started thinking about why we have the 50K or 100K rules, yet most settings seem to have (or be written for) hundreds of undead. So, I looked back at the city population (metro-wide, the ratio is something like 1 vampire: 50,000 mortals). I figure that what makes the population limits so important is not food source but the ability to remain undetected. It follows that in larger cities, between increased isolation (how many folks you know in a given area) inter-city travel (folks from all over town showing up at night spots) and increased tourism, etc., the acceptable Kindred limit should rise faster than the mortal population. I came up with a quick, conservative formula to see what the numbers might look like, and my metro area, which theoretically could comfortably support 20-40 vampires, might actually carry well over 100, assuming they behaved moderately well.<br /> <br /> I don't know what other folks think about population levels, but I wouldn't be surprised if it's been talked to death on the various fora.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T12:44:55-07:00","id":176291,"title":"","content":"I don't care about that stuff. I would rather a game be more fun than make more sense, and more vampires often makes a game more fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T13:02:09-07:00","id":176320,"title":"","content":"I think the stance I've seen people take recently (One which I approve of and generally agree with) is that the statistic isn't super relevant, and that the best idea is to play it by ear. There are as many vampires in your city as you need.<br /> <br /> All the factors you've been thinking about are good to think about too, especially in characterizing how your city's gen pop of Kindred act.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T13:34:49-07:00","id":176356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/176270-a-thought-on-vampiric-population?p=176320#post176320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the stance I've seen people take recently (One which I approve of and generally agree with) is that the statistic isn't super relevant, and that the best idea is to play it by ear. There are as many vampires in your city as you need.<br /> <br /> All the factors you've been thinking about are good to think about too, especially in characterizing how your city's gen pop of Kindred act.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right. One reason for keeping the ratio in mind in my setting is that the Ordo Dracul is trying to tie VII attacks to relative concentration of vampires.<br /> <br /> I frequently torn between having the full panoply of functioning Covenants, and having a few vampires hiding alone in the mortal world (street-level stuff). But I think I'll opt for an influx of undead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T13:39:04-07:00","id":176358,"title":"","content":"Also, I'm pretty sure that the 1/50k 1/100k is worldwide, while vampires congregate in cities.<br /> <br /> Even at 1/50k, LA (including greater LA area) would have over 350 vampires, New York would have been nearly 400. Dallas/Fort Worth would be closer to 130.<br /> <br /> Then you have vampires from nearby smaller areas gathering in the major cities. A city of 50k or 100k isn't likely to have its lone vampire for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T13:46:52-07:00","id":176380,"title":"","content":"Yeah, those statistics are meant to be a global mean, but that data should be massively skewed towards higher vampire to human ratios in densely populated areas and few-to-no vampires in sparsely populated rural areas. With such uneven distribution, Mean is a terrible indicator of Average.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T13:57:39-07:00","id":176391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corrigan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/176270-a-thought-on-vampiric-population?p=176356#post176356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're right. One reason for keeping the ratio in mind in my setting is that the Ordo Dracul is trying to tie VII attacks to relative concentration of vampires.<br /> <br /> I frequently torn between having the full panoply of functioning Covenants, and having a few vampires hiding alone in the mortal world (street-level stuff). But I think I'll opt for an influx of undead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could establish an observed average in the city based upon the last 100 or so years. Maybe it also accounts for nomads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T15:37:07-07:00","id":176466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corrigan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/176270-a-thought-on-vampiric-population#post176270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I started thinking about why we have the 50K or 100K rules</div> </div> </div> </div>It was just a suggestion for people who insist on having numbers for that sort of thing (you'll see how for every new splat or splat that doesn't specifically mention numbers, people clamor to be told the exact population numbers). I'm sure given another chance they wouldn't mention it (like they didn't in Blood and Smoke). As the true population is no more or less than however many you want in your story.<br /> <br /> There's two ways to go with it.<br /> Give a number, have people complain. They tried this, people complained.<br /> Don't give a number, have people ask. They seem to be sticking with this one, but people keep asking for numbers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T15:52:27-07:00","id":176468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/176270-a-thought-on-vampiric-population?p=176466#post176466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was just a suggestion for people who insist on having numbers for that sort of thing (you'll see how for every new splat or splat that doesn't specifically mention numbers, people clamor to be told the exact population numbers). I'm sure given another chance they wouldn't mention it (like they didn't in Blood and Smoke). As the true population is no more or less than however many you want in your story.<br /> <br /> There's two ways to go with it.<br /> Give a number, have people complain. They tried this, people complained.<br /> Don't give a number, have people ask. They seem to be sticking with this one, but people keep asking for numbers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand. I'm fine with general numbers so long as they make sense, but clearly people are going to do what they want to do. For me, it's been more of a balance between having enough interaction to feel like a society, and getting cramped.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T11:25:11-07:00","id":177204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/176270-a-thought-on-vampiric-population?p=176291#post176291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't care about that stuff. I would rather a game be more fun than make more sense, and more vampires often makes a game more fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do. But having more vampires than population can support can break the suspension of belief. Though it can suck if you are in a midsize city.<br /> The new discipline costs don't help. I know the blood banking and feeding off animal rules have been tweaked but have no sense how that affects things.<br /> Example most D&amp;D campaigns are unrealistic in that large monsters(predators) seem to abound in areas that cannot support them.<br /> <br /> Other NWoD splats don't have the same predator spot with humans so you can fudge their numbers more.<br /> Also nothing says you have to have all covenants in a city or clans. That could lead to plot on it's own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T22:55:29-07:00","id":178690,"title":"","content":"The last time I saw figures in printed material the number of active vampires in the world came out to be 1 in 50000 mortals. I looked at the world population almost as long ago and roughly half of all people live in an urban area. I assume the number of active vampires excludes any that might live in rural areas because any such vampires would be unknown, like the number of vampires in torpor. That leads me to believe that in a metro area there would be twice as many vampires as the 1:50000 ratio would suggest. It gets tricky when you consider &quot;mega cities&quot; like Los Angeles that are huge metropolitan areas with city after city and no rural area in between.<br /> <br /> I try to find the smallest political bound that contains &quot;my city&quot; and has a population density around half of the population density of the city within the area that has the largest population. I figure out how many vampires are in that area based on the world ratio to get the known vampires in the area. Then I take a list of the metro areas within the area in descending order of population. I go down the list figuring out how many vampires would be in each city going by the world ratio times two (2:50000). When the running sum of vampire populations of cities equals the total of the area, I have found all my vampire domains within the area.<br /> <br /> All smaller cities either have no real vampire presence or are part of the domain of one of the larger cities. Vampires might be granted territories in these smaller cities. It isn't much different that people living in the suburbs. If there are multiple domains close to each other and I don't want a war of princes, I combine the domains into a large one. The prince of that domain might have regents controlling the other cities.<br /> <br /> That is about as realistic as I know how to make up numbers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T06:43:32-07:00","id":178865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/176270-a-thought-on-vampiric-population?p=178690#post178690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The last time I saw figures in printed material the number of active vampires in the world came out to be 1 in 50000 mortals. I looked at the world population almost as long ago and roughly half of all people live in an urban area. I assume the number of active vampires excludes any that might live in rural areas because any such vampires would be unknown, like the number of vampires in torpor. That leads me to believe that in a metro area there would be twice as many vampires as the 1:50000 ratio would suggest. It gets tricky when you consider &quot;mega cities&quot; like Los Angeles that are huge metropolitan areas with city after city and no rural area in between.<br /> <br /> I try to find the smallest political bound that contains &quot;my city&quot; and has a population density around half of the population density of the city within the area that has the largest population. I figure out how many vampires are in that area based on the world ratio to get the known vampires in the area. Then I take a list of the metro areas within the area in descending order of population. I go down the list figuring out how many vampires would be in each city going by the world ratio times two (2:50000). When the running sum of vampire populations of cities equals the total of the area, I have found all my vampire domains within the area.<br /> <br /> All smaller cities either have no real vampire presence or are part of the domain of one of the larger cities. Vampires might be granted territories in these smaller cities. It isn't much different that people living in the suburbs. If there are multiple domains close to each other and I don't want a war of princes, I combine the domains into a large one. The prince of that domain might have regents controlling the other cities.<br /> <br /> That is about as realistic as I know how to make up numbers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone explain why this CMS logs me the logs me back in?<br /> I take a similar tact. Y'all might find this useful when doing the #'s. This is <a href=\"http://www.wolframalpha.com/input/?i=atlanta&amp;lk=4\" target=\"_blank\">what I got</a> when I punched in Atlanta into Wolfram Alpha.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T07:41:13-07:00","id":178924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/176270-a-thought-on-vampiric-population?p=177204#post177204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do. But having more vampires than population can support can break the suspension of belief. Though it can suck if you are in a midsize city.<br /> The new discipline costs don't help. I know the blood banking and feeding off animal rules have been tweaked but have no sense how that affects things.<br /> Example most D&amp;D campaigns are unrealistic in that large monsters(predators) seem to abound in areas that cannot support them.<br /> <br /> Other NWoD splats don't have the same predator spot with humans so you can fudge their numbers more.<br /> Also nothing says you have to have all covenants in a city or clans. That could lead to plot on it's own.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does not take 50,000 Humans to support one Vampire. Assuming that you fed on each of them only a single time, for one point of blood, and you fed every day, that would allow you to feed for 136.98 Years with never feeding on the same person twice. Assuming you are a <i><b>glutton</b></i>, and took 2 points of Blood, that would lead to a different, slightly anemic, slightly tired person, every day, for 68.49 Years. You could chop the ration down to 1:5000 (one Point of Blood/day from different people every day for 13.69 Years) and still have plenty of food to go around and still keep from being noticed on a continual basis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T08:17:08-07:00","id":178942,"title":"","content":"Yes, there's a problem with basing vampire populations on predators, vampire's are in no way required to act as predators, many of them get along just fine being parasites. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T12:01:05-07:00","id":179111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/176270-a-thought-on-vampiric-population?p=178942#post178942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yes, there's a problem with basing vampire populations on predators, vampire's are in no way required to act as predators, many of them get along just fine being parasites.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>really? How many only take 2 points? It takes one just to rise.<br /> Granted you want to be a shallow drinker but that is still low. Add the fact Vitae Discipline use just went up. How much time does take to extract via the kiss?<br /> I think the population totals may be more based on how many bodies can be removed from the group before noticing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T12:25:25-07:00","id":179120,"title":"","content":"In my games taking 2 is the norm because the average Stamina is 2, and taking more than that will cause a person to suffer the drained condition.<br /> <br /> That said, in desperate times, frenzying times or hungry times, sometimes we take more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T21:00:54-07:00","id":179439,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure the relatively low population of vampires to mortals has nothing to do with feeding. It is all about hiding among the masses. I think it was always about that. There really is no reason for vampires to be so rare otherwise and the whole complex social structures (e.g. covenants) is suggestive that vampires should not be so rare, or they have a short &quot;lifespan&quot; for a creature that can theoretically exist forever. There must be lots of vampires in torpor. The low numbers help make the Masquerade believable.<br /> <br /> You should skip food supply as a basis for vampire population unless you are running some kind of story with vampires are known to be real by the mortal population, at least locally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T22:49:34-07:00","id":179484,"title":"","content":"I tend to reason that the controlling factors for vampires isn't so much food supply as it is camouflage. Large amounts of kindred attract attention; from hunters, normal mortals that might turn into hunters, other supernaturals and, perhaps most troubling of all, opposing vampire groupings.<br /> Another function that might effectively limits vampire population could be territory, as they seem quite prone to claim large tracts of land, and larger swathes of the population than they actually need, as their own and also enforce such claims in some rather terrifying ways. (nightmare, cruac, protean, you name it and some creepy vampire has probably done worse).<br /> <br /> In the end however I, personally, tend to simply go with whatever works for the game, with a nod towards the fact that the less discreet the local populous the smaller the pop can be if they want to remain &quot;safe&quot;, the more discreet they are the more of them that can stick around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T00:05:47-07:00","id":179502,"title":"","content":"I agree with the thoughts on territory. Territory seems more finite than people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T03:24:12-07:00","id":179561,"title":"","content":"I tend to completely ignore anyone that writes supernatural population stuff down. There are only 666 Lucifuge? In the world? That's not enough to support a global organization. Someone told me that, in some book somewhere, it was mentioned that there are only 100 prometheans world wide. How would that even work to find a throng? Or run any of the stories in the Promethean books? <br /> <br /> It just doesn't make sense to me. Especially with vampires, and how there's widely different takes on vampires and feeding. I personally feel that its viable to have a steady herd that you maintain for your vitae, and can go decades without accidentally killing someone. Others feel that vampires are responsible for a couple deaths a year, and are ignorant if they deny it. I've encountered lots of mindsets about feeding. How territory should work - some claim large blocks or neighborhoods, others just certain buildings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T14:34:04-07:00","id":180093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/176270-a-thought-on-vampiric-population?p=179111#post179111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">really? How many only take 2 points? It takes one just to rise.<br /> Granted you want to be a shallow drinker but that is still low. Add the fact Vitae Discipline use just went up. How much time does take to extract via the kiss?<br /> I think the population totals may be more based on how many bodies can be removed from the group before noticing.</div> </div> </div> </div>My vampires, when I play, do this on a consistent basis. Minimal Blood Usage, low Combat and Minimal Discipline use tend to allow you to not need a lot of Blood. And since mine can feed on animals as well, if I really need blood, there is an abundant food source that is not human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T13:42:31-07:00","id":181204,"title":"","content":"You know, it occurs to me that Kindred populations probably wouldn't be densest in the big, modern, wealthy cities that we usually get setting books about.<br /> <br /> Throughout much of the world outside of the most affluent nations, major cities are surrounded by huge, permanent shantytowns inhabited by desperately poor people with little-to-no police protection or official documentation. Disease and violence are commonplace, and relatively large numbers of people could disappear without attracting the attention of the nation or the world at large. Plus, a monstrous predator of the night would be much less likely to run into things like security cameras and people with smartphones reporting their activities in real-time. Parts of sub-Saharan Africa in the World of Darkness, for instance, might be thick with low-Humanity vampires carrying on horrifyingly consequence-free requiems as they contribute to the spread of the debilitating blood-bourne diseases that plague the region.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T08:44:44-07:00","id":181999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/176270-a-thought-on-vampiric-population?p=179120#post179120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my games taking 2 is the norm because the average Stamina is 2, and taking more than that will cause a person to suffer the drained condition.<br /> <br /> That said, in desperate times, frenzying times or hungry times, sometimes we take more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks I keep forgetting how truncated stats are in this system. Though if you use the themes from the blood they want to use those powers because of the thrill it is to have them.<br /> Definitely pushes the masquerade to edge a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T20:31:52-07:00","id":295576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/176270-a-thought-on-vampiric-population?p=179439#post179439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure the relatively low population of vampires to mortals has nothing to do with feeding. It is all about hiding among the masses. I think it was always about that. There really is no reason for vampires to be so rare otherwise and the whole complex social structures (e.g. covenants) is suggestive that vampires should not be so rare, or they have a short &amp;quot;lifespan&amp;quot; for a creature that can theoretically exist forever. There must be lots of vampires in torpor. The low numbers help make the Masquerade believable.<br /> <br /> You should skip food supply as a basis for vampire population unless you are running some kind of story with vampires are known to be real by the mortal population, at least locally.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems to be the stance of the Blood and Smoke book.<br /> <br /> &quot;It is not merely a matter of blood volume, for even the smallesttown has enough blood to sate a vampire, but the ability to hunt unnoticed. cloud to cover in mortal mind is apathy, and apathy is achieved with ad nauseum. Face after face after face, and who can keep track of it all? Mortals have only so much love to give; that stuff don't run cheap. someone vanishes in a small town, and it is a tragedy. Someone vanished in the city, in the quagmire of media over-stimulation, and... what were we talking about again?&quot; -p63","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4176-rpggilbert","name":"rpggilbert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4176_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T19:41:36-07:00","id":298635,"title":"","content":"Maybe it should be taken into consideration that vampires aren't the only supernaturals living in the city? You've got Mages, Changelings, Werewolves (Iron Masters, anyways), Demons, and who knows what else. If you let the supernatural population get too large, it would be pretty difficult to explain how they've remained concealed all this time.<br /> <br /> <br /> Besides, with 1 vampire in every 50,000 mortals, that means the world population for vamps is about 130,000 scattered all over the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-31-2014, 10:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T19:47:24-07:00","id":298637,"title":"","content":"That's entirely at personal discretion. Gamelines can't and won't account for one another's populations since there isn't really a number ratio anymore anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T01:01:54-08:00","id":299841,"title":"","content":"Another thing to consider is population can't be based on peace-time, because peace-time can't last forever. Population control has to be based on how much feeding can be hidden during wartime, even if wartime only happens twice a century. The masquerade can not fail twice a century. The masquerade can not fail at all. So population has to be controlled with an eye towards things staying hidden even when vamps are burning blood like it was water.<br /> <br /> It's perfectly possible that there are 30, 40 years stretches when the vamp population could be literally ten times larger without it causing the slightest problem, but a smart prince doesn't base his policies on those stretches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 11-02-2014, 04:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T09:02:47-08:00","id":300037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/176270-a-thought-on-vampiric-population?p=299841#post299841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing to consider is population can't be based on peace-time, because peace-time can't last forever. Population control has to be based on how much feeding can be hidden during wartime, even if wartime only happens twice a century. The masquerade can not fail twice a century. The masquerade can not fail at all. So population has to be controlled with an eye towards things staying hidden even when vamps are burning blood like it was water.<br /> <br /> It's perfectly possible that there are 30, 40 years stretches when the vamp population could be literally ten times larger without it causing the slightest problem, but a smart prince doesn't base his policies on those stretches.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's so smart, never I've considered such a thing, and none of the books mention it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T09:25:59-08:00","id":300064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/176270-a-thought-on-vampiric-population?p=298635#post298635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it should be taken into consideration that vampires aren't the only supernaturals living in the city? You've got Mages, Changelings, Werewolves (Iron Masters, anyways), Demons, and who knows what else. If you let the supernatural population get too large, it would be pretty difficult to explain how they've remained concealed all this time.<br /> <br /> <br /> Besides, with 1 vampire in every 50,000 mortals, that means the world population for vamps is about 130,000 scattered all over the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vamps don't give shit what creatures they may or may not even know exist do.<br /> All they care about is what raises alarm in the herd. A mortal slasher can bring heat on vamps just as much as a sloppy kindred hunter.<br /> And with revenants in the picture that gets even dicier. You have to make clean kill. But headless bodies draw attention.<br /> What to do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T06:30:11-07:00","id":494696,"title":"","content":"From a logical standpoint, I think the number of Kindred a city can hide is in geometric proportion to the human population -- the ratio actually increases with the population.<br /> From a vampiric standpoint, I figure that a vampire considers the fewer vamps the better, unless the vampires can be categorized as Us and Them, in which case the more Us they can safely hold, the better. This could relate to covenants or to other factionalizations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T08:09:22-07:00","id":497448,"title":"","content":"No<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/176270-a-thought-on-vampiric-population?p=180093#post180093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My vampires, when I play, do this on a consistent basis. Minimal Blood Usage, low Combat and Minimal Discipline use tend to allow you to not need a lot of Blood. And since mine can feed on animals as well, if I really need blood, there is an abundant food source that is not human.</div> </div> </div> </div> No offense but you haven't looked at the rules for animal blood. I need to evise this this for blood smoke and its discipline cost.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/305707-what-s-the-blood-economy-like-in-your-games?p=307643#post307643\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filed